{# A machine picture in its bezel.

   `photo` is a PhotoView or none, `machine` is the MachineView it belongs to,
   and `card` selects the smaller variant. `link` is an optional target: on the
   index the whole picture is a second way into the machine's page, because a
   picture in a card reads as clickable whether or not it is one. The card's
   own text link stays where it is - this one is deliberately not hidden from
   assistive technology either, since its alt text is what says a picture is a
   generated illustration.

   Nothing is rendered under the picture — no credit, and no label on the
   generated ones. What a picture is stays in its alt text and on the credits
   page, which is where the licence obligation is met too.

   No credit is rendered here. The pictures are cartoon-filtered crops of
   freely licensed Commons photographs, and CC BY and CC BY-SA still oblige us
   to name the photographer — but they let us do it in a manner reasonable to
   the medium, which here is one credits page carrying every photographer,
   licence, source page and the note that the images were altered. It is
   linked from the footer of every page, and `image_credits.html` is generated
   from the same record this view is, so a picture cannot reach the site
   without its entry appearing there.

   `width`/`height` come off the file itself, so the box is reserved before
   the image lands and nothing below it moves. Every picture is processed to
   one shape, so those boxes are also one shape. #}
<figure class="shot">
    {% if photo %}
    <div class="bezel">
        {% if link %}<a class="shotlink" href="{{ base }}{{ link }}">{% endif %}
        <img src="{{ base }}assets/{{ photo.card_url if card else photo.url }}"
             alt="{{ photo.alt }}"
             loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             {% if card %}
             {% if photo.card_width %}width="{{ photo.card_width }}" height="{{ photo.card_height }}"{% endif %}
             {% else %}
             {% if photo.width %}width="{{ photo.width }}" height="{{ photo.height }}"{% endif %}
             {% endif %}>
        {% if link %}</a>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <div class="bezel">
        <div class="missing">
            {% if machine.family_mark_url %}
            <img class="mark" src="{{ base }}{{ machine.family_mark_url }}" alt="">
            {% endif %}
            <span>No freely licensed photograph of the {{ machine.name }} exists yet.</span>
        </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
</figure>
